2026-09-19, no migration in this push. Two jobs in one run.

**1 · STAGE 0, the measurement everything after it is sized by.** §14's staged plan
counts 27 predicate-less policies, 7 predicate-less write policies and 7 write grants
to `anon` — all of them read from MIGRATION HISTORY. `no-orphan-table`'s lesson (§4
D43) is that production can differ: a policy dropped by hand, a grant added in the
dashboard, a role that is not there. Stages 1–6 change live access control, so they
are sized from the database and not from the repo. Seven probes:

  0.1 every policy in `public`, classified — how many refuse nothing, how many name
      the GUC path, how many already name `auth.uid()`
