WP 7.1 STAGE 0, SECOND READ — two probes the first read's OUTPUT asked for
2026-09-19, no migration in this push.

Run 35466925117 came back fenced clean and moved three of §14's numbers by more than
an order of magnitude (48 predicate-less policies not 27, 16 write-covering not 7, 86
tables `anon` may write not 7 — §4 D154; and 0 of 14 approved users present in
`auth.users` — D155). Reading it showed stage 0 was missing two questions.

  0.8 **grant × RLS × policy, intersected.** Neither count above is the exposure: a
      grant matters only where RLS lets the statement through, and a predicate-less
      policy matters only where the role holds the grant. The third term is RLS
      itself, and it changes the MECHANISM — a table with `relrowsecurity = false`
      has no policy to AND a restrictive clause against, so stage 3 cannot reach it
      and only revoking the grant can. This probe's output is stage 4's worklist,
      RLS-off tables first.
  0.9 **which foreign keys to `auth.users` production STILL has.** The artifact
      records ten columns; at least one is stale, because
      `20260613000001_fix_snapshot_created_by.sql` dropped
      `policy_versions_created_by_fkey` in June and the introspector did not follow
      it. **The one that matters is `ingest_runs`**: `ingest_land_file` raises when
      its actor is NULL, by design, and writes that actor into
      `triggered_by_user_id`. With 0 of 14 approved users in `auth.users` those two
      requirements are mutually unsatisfiable, so if the key is still there every
      CSV landing by a real user aborts — a blocker under WP 6.5 (a), which is the
      package that publishes `ingest-file`. Every rehearsal passes because each one
      INSERTs its actor into `auth.users` first, which production has not done.
      **This probe FAILS the run if the key is real**, so the answer cannot be read
      as a footnote.

